tmux for coding agents. Run Codex, agy, OpenCode, Claude Code, Qoder, Kimi
Code and Cursor Agent side by side in tabs. Each tab is a task with its own
git worktree that becomes a PR, and Maestro keeps the history so you can
switch agents without losing context.

# Problem

Running modern AI coding agents across multiple parallel tasks creates friction and coordination overhead:

- Filesystem & Git Collisions: Running multiple agents in a single workspace causes dirty working trees, untracked changes, and conflicting edits.
- Session Fragmentation: Agents run in isolated terminal windows without centralized process management; closing a terminal interrupts work.
- Context Loss Across Agents: Switching between different agents (e.g., Codex, Claude Code, agy, Cursor) requires manually restating task
requirements and losing conversation history.
- Disconnected Task Lifecycles: The loop between task definition, agent execution, diff review, PR creation, and cleanup lacks unified tracking and
persistent record-keeping.

# Approach

Maestro solves this by acting as "tmux for coding agents"—combining a background daemon, a multiplexed terminal UI (TUI), and Git-native workflows:

- Task-to-Worktree Isolation: Every task tab automatically provisions and runs inside its own isolated Git worktree and branch, allowing multiple
agents to work concurrently on the same repository without file collision.
- Persistent Session Multiplexing: A background daemon manages PTY agent processes independently of the TUI. Developers can detach, reconnect, or
close the interface while agents continue executing in the background.
- Context-Preserving Agent Handoff: Maestro unifies disparate agent transcripts into a single task history and generates structured handoff briefs
(.maestro/handoff.md), enabling seamless agent switching on an existing task without losing prior context.
- End-to-End Lifecycle & Forge Integration: Integrates terminal supervision with Git forge operations (diff inspection, push, PR creation, and
merging), automatically cleaning up worktrees after merge while preserving the full task timeline and conversation history in local SQLite storage.
